ral play.\n\nReason: I chose (F, 3) because it is a move within the central 4x4 box, which is critical for long-term stability and mobility. It captures two opponent pieces (E3 and E4), flipping them to my color and creating a stronger, compact group of pieces in the center. Unlike moves on the G-row (like G4, G5, G6) or the C-square move (H, 2), (F, 3) does not risk giving the opponent easy access to corners or edges. It is slightly superior to (B, 4) as it keeps the game more centered and minimizes the opponent's counter-play options on the edges.\n\nAnswer: (F, 3)"}
